{"term":"sensible","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:616c301d96fabad7a5","definition":"Acting with or showing good sense; able to make good judgements based on reason or wisdom, or reflecting such ability.","example":"They ask questions of someone who thinks he's got something sensible to say on some matter when actually he hasn't.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["reasonable"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["commonsensible","electrosensible","extrasensible","nonsensible","oversensible","sensibilization","sensibleness","sensibly","subsensible","suprasensible","unsensible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a4b13fd440a2e6d369","definition":"Characterized more by usefulness, practicality, or comfort than by attractiveness, formality, or fashionableness, especially of clothing.","example":"I only wear high heels on formal occasions; otherwise, I prefer sensible shoes.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["commonsensible","electrosensible","extrasensible","nonsensible","oversensible","sensibilization","sensibleness","sensibly","subsensible","suprasensible","unsensible"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sensible#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8007475fcc1eb3699b","definition":"Able to be sensed by the senses or the psyche; able to be perceived.","example":"For Plato the belief in sensible objects is fallible.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["perceptible","appreciable","detectable"],"antonyms":["insensible","imperceptible","unappreciable","undetectable"],"collocations":[],"usage":"especially, formal","register":"especially, formal","wordFamily":["commonsensible","electrosensible","extrasensible","nonsensible","oversensib